<title>UK: Reuters' 1st ex-London Asia/MidEast air cargo repo.</title>
<headline>Reuters' 1st ex-London Asia/MidEast air cargo repo.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Below are the current average ex-UK to the Middle East/Asia GBP air cargo market rates per kg for a 100kg shipment, with a volume-to-weight ratio of six-to-one. Rates are inclusive of cargo fuel surcharges being applied to airlines.</p>
<p>		     Feb 6		Jan 24</p>
<p>			   ASIA-PACIFIC</p>
<p> LON-BKK	   1.04		 1.06</p>
<p> LON-HKG	   1.22		 1.23</p>
<p> LON-JAK	   1.00		 1.00</p>
<p> LON-MNL	   1.40		 1.40</p>
<p> LON-NRT	   1.95		 2.04</p>
<p> LON-SEL	   1.95		 2.02</p>
<p> LON-SIN	   1.25		 1.29</p>
<p> LON-SYD	   2.15		 2.15</p>
<p> LON-TPE	   1.15		 1.15</p>
<p>		     MIDDLE EAST</p>
<p> LON-BAH	   0.92		 0.93</p>
<p> LON-CAI	   0.80		 0.81</p>
<p> LON-DXB	   0.80		 0.81</p>
<p>		   INDIAN SUB-CONTINENT</p>
<p> LON-BOM	   0.75		 0.75</p>
<p> LON-DEL	   0.65		 0.65</p>
<p> LON-KAR	   1.05		 1.05</p>
<p>*The rates quoted in this report were obtained by Reuters journalists on a confidential basis from a range of airlines, large forwarders and smaller air cargo agents based at the three main London airports. *All prices quoted in sterling. *The tariffs represent average rates calculated from a range of prices and are indicative or current market activity. - Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
